+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool input validation protects executors and gives the model an opportunity to correct malformed calls.
+
+## Contract
+
+- The registry rejects missing required properties, wrong types and enum values with a ToolResponse describing the property and constraint without disclosing values, and passes valid input including extra properties unchanged to the executor exactly once ([validated by: rejects invalid inputs and passes valid input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L4)).
+- A function-valued definition is validated using its current resolved schema on each call ([validated by: validates each function-valued definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- An uncompilable static schema fails at registration with an error naming the tool ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema at registration with the tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L71)).
